1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,210
<i>Will you marry me?</i>

2
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:04,713
<i>You knew he was gonna say no!</i>

3
00:00:04,796 --> 00:00:07,090
<i>Well, Billy, I hope you're happy now!</i>

4
00:00:07,173 --> 00:00:08,800
<i>Karma's a bitch, you know.</i>

5
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:10,510
<i>And it's coming for you.</i>

6
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,512
[JUDE] <i>Who are you?</i>

7
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:14,305
<i>My name is Jordan. I'm your grandson.</i>

8
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:15,807
<i>- Thief!</i>
<i>- Okay, fine!</i>

9
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,434
- <i>Thief!</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>Please, calm down.</i>

10
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:18,518
<i>- I'm leaving.</i>
<i>- T…</i>

11
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:20,061
[JORDAN]<i> You could've at least</i>
<i>given me a heads-up.</i>

12
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,730
[BILLY] <i>It was wrong, okay? It was wrong.</i>

13
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:22,981
[JORDAN] <i>Tomorrow is…</i>

14
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:24,941
[BILLY]<i> It's the death anniversary</i>
<i>of our mothers.</i>

15
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,693
[JORDAN] <i>As long as I'm alive,</i>

16
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>I won't stop</i>

17
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:30,363
<i>until there's justice for you, Mom.</i>

18
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,781
[BILLY] <i>Why are you painting a bird?</i>

19
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,658
[ABI] <i>Because I want to be free.</i>

20
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:36,077
<i>From taking care of my sick mother.</i>

21
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,787
<i>My father left us.</i>

22
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,497
[BILLY] <i>By the way, I'm Billy.</i>

23
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,957
[ABI] <i>I'm a huge fan of LoveList.</i>

24
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,293
<i>- That's why I know so much about you.</i>
- [BILLY]<i> Thank you.</i>

25
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:44,252
<i>I'm Abi.</i>

26
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:45,670
<i>Abi Mercado.</i>

27
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:54,471
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

28
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:03,897
[MARIELA] 'Bi!

29
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:05,732
Is that you?

30
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:08,860
Come here already! I want to take a bath!

31
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,737
I'm so itchy!

32
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,322
Why'd you get home so late?

33
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:14,783
- Come on!
- Uh, I'm coming!

34
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:18,953
Yes, Ma. I'll just change,
then I'll head downstairs.

35
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:23,208
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

36
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:31,299
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

37
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:17,053
[ENGINE REVVING]

38
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:30,942
Val?

39
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:34,195
I know you're here.

40
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,031
[KNOCKING]

41
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:39,784
[JORDAN] Val?

42
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,664
Val, can we talk, please?

43
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:48,418
[MOUTHS] <i>Tell him I'm not here.</i>

44
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,588
[KNOCKING CONTINUES]

45
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,843
Oh, sorry. Ma'am Valerie isn't home.

46
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:10,982
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:13,151
[MUSIC STOPS]

48
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:19,240
["KULIMLIM" BY ANGELA KEN PLAYING]

49
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:40,762
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

50
00:03:55,944 --> 00:04:02,825
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

51
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:21,344
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

52
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,763
[MUSIC FADES]

53
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,682
For the utilities.

54
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,308
Mmm. Auntie Pres…

55
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,935
- I've got it.
- [PRECIOUS GIGGLES]

56
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,812
Our electric bill's pretty low this month.

57
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:32,230
- Mm-hmm?
- Mm-hmm.

58
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:35,275
I'm supposed to be the mom, right?

59
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,444
- There are two moms here.
- [PRECIOUS GIGGLING]

60
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:39,988
Go on, just keep it.

61
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:41,364
I've got something to show you.

62
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:45,576
It's been two years
since you started paying for our house.

63
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,162
- Eight years! Whoo!
- Eight years to go!

64
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:50,331
What's eight years? We can do it!

65
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,833
- You can do it!
- [BILLY GIGGLES]

66
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:53,293
- We can!
- We can!

67
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:56,671
[SIGHS HAPPILY]

68
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:58,840
You know what, Auntie Pres?

69
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:03,261
Those are the things our dad
promised us back then.

70
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:07,932
A house of our own.
Helping me finish school.

71
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:10,435
And every promise he made,

72
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,980
we're the ones fulfilling them
for ourselves now.

73
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:20,361
Do you really have no plans
to tell your brother

74
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:22,280
that your father's still alive?

75
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:27,952
No. He's been dead to us for a long time,
and he's never coming back.

76
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,538
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

77
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:32,832
He's not worth wasting time on anymore.

78
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:36,377
What I want to focus on

79
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:39,005
- is LoveList's expansion.
- [GASPS]

80
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:41,507
We've already ordered the equipment.

81
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:44,343
And we're about to start hiring again.

82
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:46,554
[BOTH SQUEALING]

83
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:47,513
Wait.

84
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:51,309
What happened to that investor
you were talking about?

85
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:55,271
I remember you said
your presentation's later, right?

86
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:57,565
Mm-hmm. It's later!

87
00:05:57,648 --> 00:06:00,526
And yeah! We really have to
close that deal, Auntie Pres.

88
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,861
We really do.

89
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:04,030
So, let's see.

90
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:05,907
- Pray for us!
- It's as good as done!

91
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,408
Congrats in advance!

92
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:08,743
- Not yet!
- I'm so proud of you.

93
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:10,244
- Thank you.
- That's great!

94
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,162
Not yet!

95
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,290
In a nutshell,

96
00:06:14,373 --> 00:06:17,168
LoveLine is our in-app dating coach

97
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,628
and support feature.

98
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:19,796
Because, to be honest,

99
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:23,674
even if you find
your perfect match on LoveList,

100
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,843
relationships can still get messy.

101
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,512
And with this feature,

102
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:31,974
we will be dealing with
issues of ghosting,

103
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:36,104
heartbreak, misunderstandings,
and cheating.

104
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,438
So it's like a hotline?

105
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:39,315
Yes. Yes, exactly.

106
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:40,525
That's correct.

107
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:43,152
With LoveLine, users who call

108
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:46,823
will receive real-time advice
and emotional support

109
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,908
from real people, not bots.

110
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:51,452
And from not just anyone.

111
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:54,622
You're getting advice from
licensed psychologists.

112
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,748
Like Billy.

113
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:56,999
Impressive.

114
00:06:57,583 --> 00:07:00,461
What if someone wants to stay anonymous?

115
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:03,005
Won't their identity be leaked?

116
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:04,048
No.

117
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:06,968
All interactions on LoveLine
are encrypted.

118
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,720
Even the support agents,

119
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,764
they can't see
any of your private information

120
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,182
unless you want them to.

121
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:18,855
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,489
- We love it.
- Oh, thank you.

123
00:07:28,573 --> 00:07:29,615
- Great.
- [WOMAN] However…

124
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:32,577
As you know, we're not
the final decision-makers.

125
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,412
We still need one more approval.

126
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:37,498
Of course. Mr. Salcedo, right?
Is he coming?

127
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:39,959
Oh, no. Actually, he resigned.

128
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:41,169
We have a new VP.

129
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:43,421
And as it happens, he's here today.

130
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:48,885
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

131
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,012
Billy, Jordan,

132
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:53,764
I'd like you to meet Mr. Alvin Ramirez.

133
00:07:54,724 --> 00:08:00,855
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,735
You've really got some nerve.

135
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,862
[MUSIC STOPS]

136
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:09,113
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [BILLY GRUNTS]

137
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:10,364
- [JORDAN] Hit him!
- [KICK LANDS]

138
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,365
- [ALVIN GROANS]
- [JORDAN] More!

139
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:12,450
What are you doing here?!

140
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,118
- [JORDAN] Hit him!
- Aren't you happy already?!

141
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,411
Isn't that enough for you?!

142
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,871
- What do you want from me?!
- [JORDAN] Get him!

143
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:18,206
[MUSIC STOPS]

144
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:20,208
Alvin?

145
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:22,877
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:23,794
Hi, Billy.

147
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,339
Hi, Jordan.

148
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:27,715
What do you mean, "Hi"?!

149
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:37,642
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:39,393
[MUSIC FADES]

151
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:44,232
AnCore Ventures has actually been
one of our target investors.

152
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:49,737
You guys invest in digital
and consumer startups, right?

153
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:54,242
I was able to meet
with Mr. Salcedo last week,

154
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,244
and it turns out you're the one
who took over.

155
00:08:56,994 --> 00:08:58,037
Yeah.

156
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,872
I guess it was a blessing in disguise.

157
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:03,376
So, Billy, had you known,

158
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,419
would you still have done
the presentation?

159
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:10,091
Ah, so you knew
this was Billy's all along?

160
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,220
Billy, don't believe anything
he's about to say--

161
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:15,304
Look.

162
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,807
Jordan. Billy.

163
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:22,687
I'm not doing this to make it up to you.

164
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:23,771
[SNICKERS]

165
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,898
I'm just doing my job.

166
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:30,570
Because I believe in you guys.

167
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:34,865
In what you guys do
and what you're about to do.

168
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,993
I just know it. I feel it.

169
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:38,786
It'll be a game-changer.

170
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:42,081
And I want our company to be part of it.

171
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:47,962
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:51,924
Then we have a deal.

173
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:52,842
Dude!

174
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,219
A-Are you serious?

175
00:09:55,303 --> 00:10:00,808
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

176
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:03,644
Thank you for your trust, Mr. Ramirez.

177
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,398
Yeah… "trust."

178
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:11,819
Go ahead. Come on, scold me.

179
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:16,490
You've been sitting there all quiet.
Cat got your tongue?

180
00:10:16,574 --> 00:10:18,492
He left you at the altar.

181
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:22,246
He ran away with his pregnant mistress.

182
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,498
Like, do we really have to do this, dude?

183
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,084
Is LoveList in trouble?

184
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:29,086
- What--
- Oops, no. Excuse me.

185
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:31,047
LoveList is stable.

186
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,256
It's actually still growing.

187
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:35,217
That's why we need their investment.
For the expansion.

188
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:40,139
I thought cheaters were
the one thing you hated most.

189
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:45,102
And now you're willing
to accept money from one?

190
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:47,146
Okay, hear me out.

191
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:50,149
What if you look at it
from a different perspective?

192
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:54,779
Think of it this way.
We're using Alvin too.

193
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:56,947
Hmm? Right?

194
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,115
It's just business.

195
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,701
You can't be too emotional about it, dude.

196
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,620
We won't get anywhere if you are.

197
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:11,087
Maybe you're still in love with him.

198
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,964
[COUGHS] What?!

199
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:16,008
He might get the wrong idea

200
00:11:16,675 --> 00:11:17,885
and then ask for a second chance.

201
00:11:17,968 --> 00:11:21,639
Come on, Jordan.
I don't care what he thinks.

202
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:24,350
The goal is to help more women,

203
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:27,561
not just here in the Philippines,
but all over the world.

204
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:29,605
Let's go global.

205
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:31,065
You've got some big ambitions, dude.

206
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:33,651
Yes! And we're going to make it happen.

207
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,406
Once LoveList becomes successful,

208
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:40,991
even Oliver will benefit from it.

209
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:46,205
You know I'd do anything for him, right?

210
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:49,542
We've lived in a waiting shed
before, remember?

211
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:55,172
And think about the women
at Angels of Grace.

212
00:11:56,549 --> 00:12:00,428
They'll all benefit
from LoveList's success.

213
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:03,764
So you think I'd just take
that away from them?

214
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:07,643
I don't care about Alvin.

215
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:09,061
But I do care about LoveList

216
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,605
and everyone whose lives
are connected to it.

217
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:17,319
I can't beat you anyway.

218
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,202
And this area will be used

219
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,913
for the operations of
LoveList's new feature,

220
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:30,082
which is LoveLine.

221
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,543
Really impressive, Billy.

222
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:33,919
Thank you.

223
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:37,006
What made you decide
to create this kind of app?

224
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:38,966
I think you already know by now

225
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:41,051
that LoveList isn't just for women

226
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:43,095
- who are looking for true love.
- Mm-hmm.

227
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,222
It's also for people who've been hurt

228
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:47,183
and are still hurting.

229
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:49,310
- [CHUCKLES]
- Yes!

230
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:53,230
Of course, it's to help people
avoid all the pain,

231
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:56,609
heartbreak, and emotional scars

232
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,903
caused by cheating men

233
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:01,697
- who leave women hanging.
- Hmm.

234
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,240
You see, Mr. Ramirez,

235
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:05,576
these two are incredibly passionate

236
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,578
- about the company.
- [BOTH CHUCKLING]

237
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:08,913
- [TONI] Of course we are!
- Sure.

238
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:13,918
We were at that wedding that
never happened. Right?

239
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,503
So yeah, we're passionate.

240
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,462
Blaire?

241
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:19,715
Blaire, could you please assist
Mr. Ramirez to the café?

242
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:21,926
- I'll meet you there.
- Uh, no, no, no. It's okay.

243
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,177
I can manage. It's just nearby.

244
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,762
Okay. Thank you.

245
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,889
[TONI CHUCKLES] Take care.

246
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:29,225
The coffee there is really strong.

247
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:30,643
Calm down.

248
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:32,561
Sorry, Billy.

249
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:35,397
We just can't forget what happened.

250
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,149
What he did.

251
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,110
Charm?

252
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:41,654
Toni?

253
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:47,326
I'm grateful for everything
you did to help me back then.

254
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:50,663
But I need that same support again

255
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:52,456
for the decision I'm making now.

256
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:56,252
We need this.

257
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:58,587
Deal.

258
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,965
Deal. Mm?

259
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:06,762
Thank you, everyone who believes
in what LoveList stands for.

260
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,431
We are looking forward to
even more success

261
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,766
with this collaboration.

262
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:13,143
So, big things are ahead for LoveList.

263
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:18,399
[APPLAUDING]

264
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:20,568
Billy, thank you.

265
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:22,695
Thank you, Alvin.

266
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:24,113
[MAN] Photo op.

267
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:30,411
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:38,961
Wow, if I were our chief,
I'd never forgive him.

269
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:40,713
He'd be canceled in my book.

270
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:43,257
That's how fearless Billy is.

271
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,302
When she has to face something,
she faces it head-on.

272
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:49,513
Just look how far she's come.

273
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:52,641
She's incredibly strong.

274
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:54,018
I've always looked up to her.

275
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:59,523
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:03,485
[MULTIPLE PHONES CHIMING]

277
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:10,534
- [MUSIC TURNS UNSETTLING]
- [PHONES KEEP CHIMING]

278
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:14,747
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

279
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:15,789
Look at this.

280
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:19,043
[INDISTINCT MURMURING]

281
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:21,545
Alvin! You better stop signing that.

282
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,797
- Gia?
- Gia?

283
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:24,965
- Let's go!
- What's going on?

284
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:25,925
What's happening?

285
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:30,888
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

286
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:32,014
[GIA GRUNTS]

287
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:35,309
Explain this!

288
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:38,896
- NOW THE GUY'S HER BUSINESS PARTNER?
- STRAIGHT OUT OF A SOAP OPERA!

289
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,522
Billy…

290
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:45,110
I understand we hurt you before,
but that was a long time ago!

291
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:48,155
We've been keeping to ourselves.
We have kids now.

292
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:49,531
- Gia.
- Why would you do this now?

293
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,492
How dare you?! Let's go!

294
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,327
Let's go!

295
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:57,790
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:15:57,873 --> 00:16:00,417
- [JORDAN] Don't let them leave!
- [PRESS] Ms. Billy!

297
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:03,504
- [PRESS CLAMORING]
- [WOMAN] <i>What's going on?</i>

298
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:04,838
[TONI] <i>Okay! Okay!</i>

299
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:08,676
- Please, calm down.
- You don't need to know.

300
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:14,348
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

301
00:16:14,431 --> 00:16:16,475
Boom, karma.

302
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,435
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]

303
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:21,021
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,731
Alvin, wait! Gia!

305
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:25,359
I never posted that video even back then!

306
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,820
So why did you repost it now?

307
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,446
- Billy.
- What?!

308
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:30,781
[GIA] You see?

309
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,659
It's reposted on your account.

310
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,202
I didn't do that.

311
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:37,830
[BILLY] Obviously, it was
hacked! That's not me.

312
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,040
You know, Billy,

313
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,459
trying to reconnect
with you was a mistake.

314
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:46,046
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,339
Deal is off.

316
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:48,257
[GIA] Let's go.

317
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,676
Alvin, wait. Let's talk about this.

318
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:52,803
- Let's go.
- Hey, be our convoy, okay?

319
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:54,680
It's not…

320
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,181
- [CAR ENGINE STARTS]
- It's okay.

321
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:57,433
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

322
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:06,859
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:16,660
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

324
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:28,464
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

325
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,265
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

326
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:39,391
Billy.

327
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:43,145
Billy, take a look at the comments.

328
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:45,189
[TONI] Almost all of them are positive.

329
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,274
The netizens are in your favor.

330
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,318
[CHARM] But that's not the point.

331
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,945
The point is that someone
hacked Billy's account

332
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,323
and sabotaged our deal with Alvin,

333
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:56,867
which is a big blow
to LoveList's expansion.

334
00:17:57,951 --> 00:17:58,869
[JORDAN] Guys.

335
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:01,330
You have to see this.

336
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:06,710
[BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

337
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:09,546
There's a lot of comments
being posted in LoveSpeak.

338
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,132
[JORDAN] They're throwing hate on us.

339
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:14,551
We must have been hacked.

340
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:17,930
THIS APP IS SO USELESS!

341
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:22,893
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

342
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:26,563
LET'S STOP USING THIS APP!

343
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:31,819
The accounts don't have
profile pictures or identification.

344
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:33,237
Those accounts are not verified,

345
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,197
which means they're not our members.

346
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:39,326
OMG, we're being attacked by trolls!

347
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:42,746
What if we lose members because of this?

348
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,665
[JORDAN] Okay! It's okay now.

349
00:18:44,748 --> 00:18:47,334
I've shut down their access point.

350
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,878
I also blocked their IP address.

351
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,673
But, Billy, we're still not safe.

352
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:55,050
He can reroute
through a different access point

353
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,385
and hit us again.

354
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,971
Not until we find this hacker.

355
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,890
Who would even do this?

356
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:06,603
I mean, who would hack into our system
and hack into your account?

357
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,022
[MARJ] Isn't it obvious?

358
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:11,108
It has to be Valerie.

359
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,109
[PHONE CHIMES]

360
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,028
Wow, guys.

361
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:17,447
She's even livestreaming.

362
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:20,742
Excuse me.

363
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,537
You know, guys,

364
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,165
with Ms. CEO's recent issue,

365
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:29,543
I'm not surprised if some people
are angry with her.

366
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:30,544
I mean,

367
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:33,338
<i>I just hope her company won't be affected</i>

368
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,507
<i>because I'll feel sorry for them.</i>

369
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:37,426
[VALERIE COOS INSINCERELY]

370
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:40,888
<i>But anyways, enough of this negativity.</i>

371
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:41,972
<i>That makes people uglier.</i>

372
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:44,683
<i>So now, it's time for my stress-reliever.</i>

373
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:46,185
<i>Miss, please start already.</i>

374
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,311
<i>- Okay, ma'am.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

375
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:48,312
[FRUSTRATED WHINE]

376
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:50,355
See? She's really behind this!

377
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:51,732
Hold me back, hold me back!

378
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:53,233
- I swear!
- Relax, relax.

379
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,568
We're not yet sure of that.

380
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,279
Val isn't answering.

381
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,741
I'll try her condo.

382
00:20:01,325 --> 00:20:02,826
No, no, no! Don't.

383
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,411
I know where she is.

384
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:05,454
This is in Greenbelt.

385
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:06,955
- [MARJ SQUEALS]
- Where's Billy?

386
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,669
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:15,339
[VALERIE] Guys, I had such
a big problem earlier.

388
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:17,466
While I was at the store earlier,

389
00:20:17,549 --> 00:20:20,969
it was so hard to choose between
the pink or the yellow bag.

390
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:24,932
[VALERIE] So I ended up
getting both of them.

391
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:26,892
I'll show you them later,

392
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:29,186
and let me know if I got the right choice,

393
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:31,939
if I got both of them right, or…

394
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:34,942
I think I should've just got the pink one,
but I don't know, the yellow--

395
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,402
Okay, please stop recording
for just five minutes.

396
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:39,905
Oh, look!

397
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:41,573
It's the famous CEO.

398
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:44,826
Famous for all the wrong reasons.

399
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:48,956
We've been trying to call you,
but you weren't answering.

400
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:51,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:54,544
Did you have anything to do with
LoveList getting hacked?

402
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,297
As well as my account?

403
00:20:58,131 --> 00:21:00,717
Oh, so I'm a hacker now.

404
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,137
Brilliant, wow.

405
00:21:04,221 --> 00:21:06,723
Does this face look like a hacker to you?

406
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:09,059
[VALERIE] Sweetie,

407
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:11,937
the only thing I hack is my diet.

408
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:14,690
I'm not saying that
you hacked us yourself.

409
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:18,610
What I'm asking
is if you had anything to do with it.

410
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:20,988
Paid someone to do it.

411
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,992
Can't you see I'm busy?

412
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:28,036
The damage those hackers did
to my company is no joke.

413
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:34,459
So we'll investigate
and take legal action as needed.

414
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:37,170
Go!

415
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:40,299
Karma's a bitch, isn't it?

416
00:21:40,924 --> 00:21:43,552
What, am I the only person with
a grudge against you?

417
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:46,638
Am I your only enemy?
Are you sure about that?

418
00:21:48,473 --> 00:21:51,268
I heard someone spray-painted
"Bitch" on your car,

419
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:54,521
which is something that really suits you.

420
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:57,024
Will you accuse me of doing that too?

421
00:21:57,107 --> 00:22:01,111
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

422
00:22:01,194 --> 00:22:03,447
As you can see,

423
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:05,157
I've moved on.

424
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,325
I mean, look.

425
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:08,035
I'm enjoying my time with retail therapy.

426
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:09,911
Or I was, until you ruined my day.

427
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:12,581
Now, you're making up stories.

428
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:14,833
That's why your ex-fiancé left you.

429
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,753
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

430
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:19,004
Oh well.

431
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:21,298
Like mother, like daughter.

432
00:22:22,174 --> 00:22:24,134
Your father left her too, right?

433
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:29,014
- [VALERIE GROANS]
- [MAN, WOMAN] Ma'am! Ma'am!

434
00:22:29,097 --> 00:22:31,058
[BILLY] You don't go there!

435
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:34,436
- Dude!
- [VALERIE GRUNTS]

436
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:35,479
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

437
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:40,192
- [VALERIE WAILING]
- Valerie, are you all right?

438
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:42,444
[VALERIE] This nose isn't cheap!

439
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,946
You're gonna pay for this!

440
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:49,743
[VALERIE CRYING]

441
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:57,375
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

442
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:04,883
[BILLY] <i>Do you think we can</i>
<i>track down the hacker?</i>

443
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:06,927
[JORDAN] <i>We're gonna</i>
<i>fix this. Trust me.</i>

444
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,428
[PRECIOUS] <i>We have a visitor.</i>

445
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:11,181
[ABI] <i>I saw what happened</i>
<i>with LoveList.</i>

446
00:23:11,264 --> 00:23:14,726
<i>I'm just mad at people</i>
<i>who can't fight without hiding.</i>

447
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:17,479
<i>Oliver's Family Day will be</i>
<i>this Saturday, okay?</i>

448
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,064
<i>Don't forget about it.</i>

449
00:23:19,147 --> 00:23:22,651
[MAN] <i>Just tell me if you want</i>
<i>to hack LoveList again.</i>

450
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:24,694
<i>I got his location!</i>

451
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,863
<i>I'm outside the troll's house.</i>

452
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:28,657
<i>You're going too far!</i>

453
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:29,491
[MAN] <i>Hey!</i>

454
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:33,245
<i>- I said give that to me!</i>
<i>- Get off me! Help!</i>
